            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Sanskrit for a building, then the Sanskrit for lodging."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: पृथिवी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पृथिवी — pṛthivī — \"the earth\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pṛthivī is the feminine of pṛthu, \"broad, wide\" (MW): the earth is \"the broad, extended one\". MW compares pṛthu with Greek platys, \"broad\", and English plate, so the word is inherited from Indo-European."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
