          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "jagat is a reduplicated form of the root √gam, \"to go\" (MW): \"moving, living\". In the Rigveda it means \"men and animals\", and in the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa \"the world\" (CDIAL 5078): the world as everything that moves."
            }
          ]
        },
